Z||000008||Cooter||07-05-99||07:56 PM||||DXR-Will- I think that says it all! I believe that the reason Baskin Robins has 31 flavors is because people like different stuff, what a dull world it would be if everyone thought/did the same (unless it involved Fiero's!!)
Z||000009||four50four||07-05-99||08:17 PM||||i hate stickers! the only place the belong is in the garbage or on a tool box. first thing i do whenever i buy a car, truck, motorcycle, etc. is remove whatever ugly stickers the previous owner had on it. when i see a fiero two things come to mind, performance and a certian degree of class that comes from this type of sports car. i see it with the big cars like the corvette and the european makes. honestly, have you ever seen a really high performance mid-engine car with stickers on it? i haven't and i hope i never will. you see the little fiero is different from all the other detroit muscle machines it has class and it doesn't deserve to be covered up with ugly stickers.<p><br>ps. i have seen speed stripes on a dodge omni and a chevy spirit. trust me they don't make you go faster!
Z||000010||ChadMan||07-06-99||07:10 AM||||I have seen some fast, fast Hondas (1/4 mi in 13.5 to 15.0), but for every truly quick Honda, I've seen 50 of the stickers-n-stereo boys whose only performance mod is a sewer-pipe exhaust tip.<p>The fastest Honda I've seen in person was an '87 Civic 4-dr with a hopped-up Integra motor in it.  No stripes, no stickers, just a mild tint and some factory CRX wheels.  Now that's a sleeper.
Z||000011||Racer 1||07-06-99||12:31 PM||||DXR_WILL if you read my topic I said I think there ugly.Which means thats my opinion and wouldnt tell the people with all the stickers there rides ugly.Its easy to get a sticker pack from any company and plaster them on your car if you were a wanabe.Like when you see edlebrock and holley carbs on the same car you know hes faking it!I like it when I get to a stop light and see these half ton of sticker rice bunners reving there engines at my fiero to race.Then when the light turns green seeing them barely squeal there wheels at the start while I take off slow and think to myself damn this guy is gonna need parts soon doing that stuff.One guy even broke down acouple a feet after he burned out at the stop light I rolled by laughing.
Z||000012||FieroMike||07-06-99||01:57 PM||||All my stickers are under the deck-lid.  But I have two silver stripes running up the middle of the car.  Looks pretty nice!!
Z||000013||Hock||07-08-99||01:55 PM||||Wow, in this heated debate I just can't stand to leave my opion out. Well here I go! Those stikers on those rice burners don't impress me all that much. All of mine will be under the deck lid. Now if you want to talk about exhaust systems, I was out in Mechanicsburg PA over the weekend and heard alot of rice burners with sewage pipe to the coffee can exhaust tips on them and they sound like a bumble bee. 90% of them were stock and had little punks for drivers. I mean you can have a loud exhaust on anything and it doesn't make it go fast. Hell, my Bronco II had a loud exhaust and it got beat by all king of cars. From what I have learned if you want a fast car you better forget about a loud exhaust system and stickers and start at the heart of the system.
Z||000014||PaUL||07-08-99||05:55 PM||||I also think stickers on the outside are ugly. I have all mine on the inside of the decklid too but I dont like to show them to anyone. I prefer my exterior finish to be monochrome and super shiny with no stickers. A few years ago I got my fiero painted with Dupont Imron paint. I never heard of it but the guy who painted my car said it would produce the highest gloss. When he was done, I couldnt believe it, it was the shiniest paint Id ever seen. It actually reflected sunlight like a mirror and this was the color black. I was happy with it until I hit a large dog and shattered the paint on the front facia.
Z||000015||Punkndrublic||07-08-99||09:45 PM||||I think the real problem with stickers is all the wannabes that go out and buy then put on stickers advertising stuff they don't even remotely have on their car. Then most people can't even affix the stickers of stuff they do have to the car properly, their either faded riped or crooked, and know nothing of balance and symmetry. And whats even worse is putting them on some junker as if to make it look better. Other then that a FEW nicely place small stickers(on the rear window) to what you do have or anything else for that matter really couldn't hurt. Cars are like women and fall victim to more's law. There are those who pack on the make-up and belong in the parking lot of some cheap motel and those who know what their doing and make your head turn as you drive by.
Z||000016||RFMike||07-08-99||10:17 PM||||The only sticker I have ever put on any vehicle I have owned was a very small one on a 1976 Moto Guzzi that I bought new. It was about 2 1/2" square and said, "If you like living as much as I like this motorcycle, don't #$^& with it."  I think I need to find one for my Fiero, after all the parking lot bs I've had lately.
Z||000017||lowCG||07-08-99||10:49 PM||||I need to find a couple of stickers to place on the black plastic panels just behind the side windows,at the same time I will buff off the factory decals on the decklid.<br>Any cool ideas?  Maybe a Clay Smith roadrunner,or some mOOn eyes?   <br>This could take some time.
Z||000018||theogre||07-09-99||12:24 AM||||Ok. Ok. I'll bite..............<p>First of all, I think it's lame to pay to advertise for people who make more than all of us combined. If they can't give me a decal with their product I sure as hell ain't buying one. ((Thrush Mufflers used to come with a cute little sticker, about half again the size of a silver $)) I have to like the product allot or even then the sticker ain't goin' on the car. I'll stuff it on a tool box or something, maybe.<p>Here in Delaware, The Vanity State, Home of Brain Free Driving, we have more boom boxes on go carts than I can count. Very few of them are worth looking at, or listening to.  Any jackass can slog speakers and amplifiers into a car these days and call it good sound..... shows how deaf most americans must be..... We also have lots of swollen bee's running around. Talk about cars with a case of gas...... FFFFFFFFFFFFAAAAAAAAAAAARRRRRRRRRRRTTTTTTTTTTTTT!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡ The really funny ones tho are the low rider builders that basically chop out the suspension. Nothing funnier that a pingpong car with the front end blown apart from separated ball joints stuck in the middle of the parkway. Made the whole traffic tie up worth the wait for that laugh.<p>The most anoying thing with stickers, including stripe tape, is that the things look old fast. Even the high grade factory logos & stripes look like hell long before the car needs repainting. Not to many things uglier than old decals.<p>So far the only way I think you can get them safely off Fiero is with a hair dryer, a Very good razor blade, and allot of time. Don't try to just buff them off, you'll likely eat the paint off around them first, the sticker is far thicker than the paint. I haven't tried things like some of the chemical sticker pealers that are fairly new to market, I'm worried they may also attack the plastic pannels. I definatly wouldn't use the Oven Cleaner method on plastic pannels. It worked good most of the time on metal tho with todays new paints, it could be trouble.<p>As for things like Boom Cars, and low riders, there is a growing ammount a legislation in many U.S. areas that will affect them. The top 2 rules are noise ordinances, and expansion of special vehical inspections. Here in my county if you drive with a boom car with the volume turned up, you can be stopped for it and ticketed. Do it after 9-10PM and you are a ticket magnet. In N.J.(I think) if you have a modified, I.E. jacked, truck/SUV, you are required to pass a special inspection that looks for things like wooden blocks, and Hockey Pucks, used as lifts. Don't laugh.... The jacked freak behind you may easily have such things holding up the pig.... A number of states are looking at these inspection rules for jacked and lowered cars. The primary reasons are that major assholes are doing most of this work, and the fact that there is effectivly NO safety certification of jacking/lowering products.<p>The shame of such things is that for every car/truck you get that's truly well done there are 50 that are crap. It makes the well done ones look bad too.
Z||000019||Racer 1||07-09-99||03:36 PM||||UM TheOrge I dont mean to burst your bubble on ya post as I agree to most of it.But I have lots of speekers in my ride and like LOUD music but respect people after dark and keep the sound down.Most lower riders around here have the nicest rims and tires with primered paint job and bounce severly down the road do to lack of rear springs in the back kinda makes me sick looking at them especialy when I see a coke in there hands while there bouncing!!LOL
Z||000020||theogre||07-09-99||09:10 PM||||burst what bubble...... Like I said... for every one good one there are 50 morons. It makes the few good ones look like jerks too allot of the time. A thing which rather stinks.
